     "text": "{\"count\": 4, \"rationale\": \"Answer: 4, for example by blocking dbReplica:collection, codeRepo:collection, shareMount:collection and mailArchive:collection. These are all four parents of the OR target, so blocking them leaves the target unreachable.\\n\\nWhy 3 is not enough: there are four attack paths to the target that share no blockable step.\\n1. phishing → browserStore → fileServer → mailArchive → target.\\n2. wifiGuest → kerberoast → backupHost → codeRepo → target.\\n3. wifiGuest → sshKey → jumpHost → shareMount → target.\\n4. internet → workstation, and wifiGuest → ciRunner, both feeding the AND step ssoLogin → monitoringHost → dbReplica → target.\\n\\nEach path is fully reachable by itself from the footholds. Because no blockable step appears in more than one path, a single block stops at most one of them. So at least 4 blocks are needed.\"}"
    }
